WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:04.720
Whether they came from veteran actors at&nbsp;
the height of their career or rising stars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:09.280
taken too soon, last words can leave an&nbsp;
impact on many. These are some of the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:13.840
heart wrenching final exchanges actors&nbsp;
have shared with their late co-stars.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:19.960
Desi Arnaz was as big as they come throughout his&nbsp;
acting career, which spanned from 1940 until his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:26.080
final film role in 1982's The Escape Artist.&nbsp;
More famously, Arnaz was recognized for being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:32.000
the lead in the groundbreaking 1950s sitcom I&nbsp;
Love Lucy, alongside his then-wife Lucille Ball.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.600
The pair met on the set of the film&nbsp;
Too Many Girls and eloped during the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.320
movie's production. Together,&nbsp;
the couple filmed more than 180&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:43.840
episodes of I Love Lucy while going on&nbsp;
to make films and special appearances.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:46.040
"I think if it wouldn't have been for Lucy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:50.920
I would stopped trying a long time ago&nbsp;
because I was always the guy that didn't fit."

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:55.520
Unfortunately, the world's most famous&nbsp;
couple of the time divorced in 1960,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.520 --> 00:01:00.040
and shared few exchanges until&nbsp;
Arnaz was on his deathbed in 1986.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:05.240
The 2022 documentary Lucy and Desi revealed&nbsp;
many truths about the Hollywood couple,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:09.800
including their final words to each other.&nbsp;
According to their daughter, Lucie Arnaz, she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:16.240
reunited her parents to have one last conversation&nbsp;
on their wedding anniversary, November 30, 1986.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:21.800
Realizing Arnaz’s time was limited, the former&nbsp;
partners spoke on the phone. Ball reportedly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:28.520
exclaimed her love for her former co-star, and he&nbsp;
replied in kind. Arnaz passed away two days later.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:33.640
Most famous for performing ridiculous daredevil&nbsp;
acts as a regular cast member on Jackass,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:36.880
MTV reports that Ryan Dunn was known as the cast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:41.040
member willing to take on stunts&nbsp;
even the likes of Steve-O wouldn't.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:46.040
A longtime member of the troupe, Dunn was&nbsp;
undeniably closest with star Bam Margera,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:51.600
since the pair had worked alongside each other in&nbsp;
the Jackass predecessor series CKY. Unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:55.880
in 2011, Dunn and his production&nbsp;
assistant Zachary Hartwell died in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.880 --> 00:02:00.120
an alcohol-involved vehicular accident&nbsp;
in Chester County, Pennsylvania.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:05.240
Torn up about the loss of his friend, Margera&nbsp;
spoke about the accident with E! News a short&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:10.200
time later. He called Dunn his best friend, and&nbsp;
explained that he was still in extreme pain over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:15.480
the loss five days after the tragic accident.&nbsp;
Sadly, the former co-star then revealed the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:20.880
troubling final text message that he received from&nbsp;
Dunn on the night of the fateful crash. It read,

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:23.280
"Stopping for a beer, be there when I can."

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:28.080
What weighed on Margera even further was the&nbsp;
fact that he had been in a similar accident&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:34.160
with Dunn 15 years prior. He recalled that,&nbsp;
in 1996, Margera flipped a car several times&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:39.320
on the same stretch of road and Margera&nbsp;
considered himself lucky to have survived.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:44.680
Redd Foxx was a celebrated comedian best&nbsp;
known for his 1970s sitcom Sanford and Son.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:49.560
The prominent stand-up's influence can still&nbsp;
be seen in comedy today thanks to his long,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:51.960
illustrious career and many catchphrases.

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:57.280
In 1991, the seasoned 68-year-old actor&nbsp;
plotted a television comeback and began&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:01.120
work on a new sitcom called The&nbsp;
Royal Family. However, he died&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:05.920
before the series could air under extremely&nbsp;
unfortunate and unforeseen circumstances.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:08.560
Foxx suffered a massive heart&nbsp;
attack while rehearsing for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:12.240
the upcoming sitcom. His co-star&nbsp;
and friend of over four decades,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:17.440
Della Reese, was caught off guard by the genuine&nbsp;
health troubles, as Foxx would often fake heart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:22.120
troubles while grabbing his chest and joking&nbsp;
that he was having a serious health scare.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:27.360
​"This is the worst one I ever had, son. Oh&nbsp;
it's the worst one, this is the big one!"

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:31.840
Reese told Jet that Foxx was already doing&nbsp;
a bit when the heart attack struck, so she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:36.280
assumed his actions were purposeful.&nbsp;
Sadly, Redd fell to the floor and,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:40.800
unable to adhere to witnesses' requests&nbsp;
that he get up, he uttered his last words:

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:42.360
"I can't breathe."

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:46.640
Award-winning actor John Ritter was a star&nbsp;
of movies and television. In the legendary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:51.640
sitcom Three's Company, Ritter played the&nbsp;
lead role of Jack Tripper for more than 170&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:56.040
episodes. Alongside a slew of other television&nbsp;
appearances, the actor was still at the top&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:01.600
of his game in the early 2000s as the dad in 8&nbsp;
Simple Rules... For Dating My Teenage Daughter.

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:06.880
Tragically, Ritter died abruptly in 2003&nbsp;
while filming the sitcom, much to the shock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:11.480
of co-star Kaley Cuoco, who would later go&nbsp;
on to play Penny on The Big Bang Theory.

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:15.880
Remembering her on-screen father, Cuoco&nbsp;
spoke about her time filming 8 Simple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:20.360
Rules with Ritter on the 15th anniversary of&nbsp;
his passing. She admitted that even though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:24.320
many years have gone by since his death,&nbsp;
her love for the actor is still strong.

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:29.120
In her final moments with the sitcom veteran,&nbsp;
Cuoco asked Ritter how he was feeling, having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:35.160
heard he was sick. In a very fatherly manner,&nbsp;
he sat Cuoco down and told her he loved her.

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:38.840
"And I was like, 'I love you, too, silly&nbsp;
man.' He goes, 'No, I want you to know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:42.080
I love you.' And I said, 'I love&nbsp;
you too.' And he goes, 'That's it!'"

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:45.880
The pair then embraced, and that was&nbsp;
the last time they would interact.

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:51.000
Famed actress Natasha Richardson was the&nbsp;
daughter of Emmy Award winner Vanessa Redgrave&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:55.840
and a member of England's Redgrave family&nbsp;
dynasty. Richardson made a name for herself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.840 --> 00:05:00.240
in films such as Gothic and The Handmaid's&nbsp;
Tale, before meeting the love of her life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:04.680
Liam Neeson, during a Broadway&nbsp;
production of Anna Christie in 1993.

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:08.120
Their relationship quickly flourished,&nbsp;
and they would go on to collaborate on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:12.600
further projects and welcome two&nbsp;
children. Unfortunately, in 2009,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:17.760
the actress suffered a fatal head injury&nbsp;
during a skiing accident in Quebec, Canada.

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:20.240
Years later, during an episode of 60 Minutes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:24.640
Neeson shared the harrowing final moments&nbsp;
he spent with his wife. Before being taken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:28.200
to the hospital with a significant&nbsp;
blood clot, Richardson told him,

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.640
"Oh darling, I've taken a tumble in the snow."

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:35.280
When Neeson arrived to be beside his wife,&nbsp;
Richardson was no longer conscious and her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:39.760
husband was forced to make a difficult decision.&nbsp;
He explained to 60 Minutes that he and Richardson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:44.240
had promised if either was ever in a, quote,&nbsp;
"vegetative state," their partner would take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:49.440
them off life support. Neeson honored his wife's&nbsp;
wish, and recalled to 60 Minutes that he informed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:54.280
an unresponsive Richardson of his decision,&nbsp;
though he was unsure if she could hear him.

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:59.120
A stand-up comedy legend, Bob Saget is&nbsp;
best remembered for his work in television.

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:02.320
"Kids, I'm gonna tell you an incredible story."

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:08.040
He provided the narrating voice of Ted Mosby for&nbsp;
more than 200 How I Met Your Mother episodes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:12.520
and hosted nearly another 200 episodes of&nbsp;
the video clip series America's Funniest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:17.160
Home Videos. Still, Saget remains most&nbsp;
famous for his role as Danny Tanner on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:21.360
the long-running sitcom Full House,&nbsp;
and its sequel series Fuller House.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:25.480
While the characters of Full House learned&nbsp;
how to become a family through eight seasons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:29.840
the performers playing the roles created&nbsp;
their own lifelong connections. Tragically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:35.880
Saget's January 2022 passing helped audiences&nbsp;
realize just how close the actors of Full House&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:40.880
were. Many of his co-stars spoke out about the&nbsp;
interactions they had with Saget late in life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:45.880
but his onscreen daughter Candice Cameron&nbsp;
Bure's recollection was particularly touching.

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:50.400
Speaking with Today, Cameron Bure recalled&nbsp;
that she and Saget had plans to meet up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:54.480
shortly before his passing, but a delayed&nbsp;
flight and a small argument prevented them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:58.880
from meeting. The next day, Saget sent her&nbsp;
a long, heartfelt message expressing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:03.080
deep affection he had for his co-star.&nbsp;
He rounded out the text with the words,

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:07.120
"I love you more for the trouble you're&nbsp;
giving me. If that's even possible."

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:11.720
Without question, Elvis Presley ranks as the&nbsp;
biggest rock star of his time, and is often&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.720 --> 00:07:16.840
regarded as one of the most influential people of&nbsp;
the 20th century. The hip-shaking singer became an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:22.200
international sensation for his groundbreaking,&nbsp;
best-selling music that crossed multiple genres.

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:26.520
Launching to stardom in the mid-1950s,&nbsp;
Presley dominated the charts until his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:32.000
shocking death in August 1977 – although,&nbsp;
his influence is still felt today. During&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:36.680
Presley's revolutionary career, audiences all&nbsp;
over the world clamored to see the King of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:41.240
Rock and Roll perform. His natural charisma&nbsp;
helped him make the transition into acting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:44.520
and he quickly emerged as one of&nbsp;
Hollywood's biggest movie stars.

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:51.560
Between 1956 and 1969, Presley starred in&nbsp;
31 feature films ranging from westerns to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:55.400
romances that almost always included&nbsp;
original musical numbers. Some of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:59.560
his most famous roles involved the&nbsp;
utopian island backdrop of Hawaii,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:05.600
which is where he met co-star Irene Tsu on&nbsp;
the set of 1966's Paradise, Hawaiian Style.

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:09.720
Speaking with Fox News, Tsu recalled&nbsp;
that they formed a close bond on set,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:13.200
sharing interests in spirituality&nbsp;
and martial arts. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:17.640
it was her last interaction with The King that&nbsp;
resonated most for the actor. She recalled,

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:19.840
"He just looked at me and&nbsp;
said, 'Keep that light burning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:23.520
baby,' and that was it. I guess he lost&nbsp;
his light. Couldn't find his way home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:28.360
you know? I truly feel he just worked&nbsp;
himself to death. It was very tragic."

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:33.000
An icon of classic cinema, Humphrey Bogart&nbsp;
helped Hollywood become what it is today&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:38.480
thanks to performances in timeless films such as&nbsp;
Casablanca, The Maltese Falcon, and The African&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:43.201
Queen. In life, he was responsible for one of&nbsp;
the most iconic lines in cinematic history.

00:08:43.201 --> 00:08:46.120
"Here's looking at you, kid."

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:50.200
However, as important as he was to the film&nbsp;
industry, the same attention could be given to his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:55.440
longtime wife and superstar actress Lauren Bacall.&nbsp;
The pair met on the set of Bacall's first film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.440 --> 00:09:00.680
To Have and Have Not, and despite a 25-year age&nbsp;
gap, they hit it off. They married soon after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:05.200
and went on to co-star in several movies,&nbsp;
including The Big Sleep and Key Largo.

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:09.200
Bogart and Bacall's marriage remains&nbsp;
one of Hollywood's truest love stories.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:13.160
The hardened Bogart reportedly shed&nbsp;
tears the day he wed his young bride,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:16.280
and they remained happily together&nbsp;
until his health deteriorated.

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:21.240
Bogart was ill for the last few years of his life,&nbsp;
but he had Bacall and many celebrity friends at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:26.200
his side. A longstanding rumor suggests that&nbsp;
Bogart's final words were, "I should never have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:31.720
switched from scotch to martinis," which sounds&nbsp;
very on brand for the actor's witty vernacular.

00:09:31.720 --> 00:09:36.240
However, it is better documented that Bogart&nbsp;
spoke last to his wife, telling Bacall,

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:37.680
"Goodbye, kid. Hurry back."

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:41.200
The actress reportedly left his&nbsp;
bedside to attend to their children,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:44.920
but Bogart slipped into a fatal&nbsp;
coma before she could return.

00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:49.960
No one can deny Sean Connery's impact&nbsp;
on cinema. The former James Bond actor's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.960 --> 00:09:54.480
monumental career spanned more than half a&nbsp;
century. He collected plenty of awards and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:58.560
acclaim while performing in numerous&nbsp;
beloved films, including Highlander,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:02.040
The Hunt for Red October, and&nbsp;
Indiana Jones and the Last Crusade.

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:06.040
The celebrated actor retired in the&nbsp;
mid-2000s, turning down substantial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:10.720
roles in both The Lord of the Rings and&nbsp;
Harry Potter franchises. Thankfully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:15.920
Connery reportedly enjoyed retirement until&nbsp;
his October 2020 passing at the age of 90.

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:20.720
Connery's legacy made a lasting impression&nbsp;
on many performers, including his co-star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:26.080
from The Untouchables, Andy Garcia. Garcia, who&nbsp;
has had a more-than illustrious career himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:30.640
wrote an article for The Hollywood Reporter&nbsp;
in memory of his old friend days after his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:34.240
passing. He even called Connery his&nbsp;
inspiration for becoming an actor.

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:38.600
Regrettably, Garcia noted that he had&nbsp;
not seen his co-star and hero for many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:43.000
years before Connery passed, despite an&nbsp;
open invitation. He wrote about the last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:47.280
time they saw each other at an event for&nbsp;
the American Film Institute, recalling,

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:50.520
"We had a cocktail or two, and it&nbsp;
was a beautiful thing. He lived in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:53.800
the Bahamas. He said, 'Come to&nbsp;
Nassau. We'll play some golf.'"

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:59.400
Garcia never did take him up on that invitation,&nbsp;
and he wrote that he continues to regret it.

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:04.600
With a personality even larger than the characters&nbsp;
that he portrayed on television, Leslie Jordan was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:10.560
a beloved public figure until his unexpected&nbsp;
death in October 2022. Small in stature and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:15.960
speaking with a thick Southern drawl, Jordan was&nbsp;
easily recognizable in his onscreen appearances.

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:19.960
Some of his most notable work includes&nbsp;
appearances in the American Horror Story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:24.560
franchise, a recurring role on Boston&nbsp;
Legal, an Emmy Award-winning guest spot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:29.200
on the NBC sitcom Will &amp; Grace, and the show&nbsp;
he co-starred on at the time of his death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:33.440
Call Me Kat. In addition to his TV work,&nbsp;
the performer gained a significant social&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:37.840
media following thanks to his comedic&nbsp;
posts during the Covid-19 pandemic.

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:41.680
Jordan's passing at the age of&nbsp;
67 shocked his fans, friends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:45.920
and co-stars. Actor Max Greenfield,&nbsp;
best known for the sitcom New Girl,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:51.240
shared a long friendship with Jordan after the&nbsp;
pair met on the set of Will &amp; Grace in 2017.

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:55.760
Greenfield missed his last opportunity to&nbsp;
see his former co-star just days before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.760 --> 00:11:59.600
Jordan died. In an interview with&nbsp;
E! News, he explained that Jordan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:03.920
attempted to visit him during a sold&nbsp;
out book signing. Greenfield recalled,

00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:08.720
"He texted me during, he was like, 'I saw — I&nbsp;
tried to get in. I saw that you were so famous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:12.400
they wouldn't let me in. They turned&nbsp;
— they turned my little a-- away.'"

00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:18.400
A pure film and music dynamo, Australian actor and&nbsp;
singer Olivia Newton-John had a fruitful career in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:22.680
both industries. As a singer-songwriter,&nbsp;
she scooped up four Grammy Awards,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:28.400
dished out a collection of Top 100 singles, and&nbsp;
landed the top entry of Billboard's Greatest of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:33.240
All Time Songs of the '80s with "Physical."&nbsp;
Meanwhile, in Hollywood, she most memorably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.240 --> 00:12:39.720
starred as leading lady Sandy in the 1978 musical&nbsp;
sensation Grease opposite a young John Travolta.

00:12:39.720 --> 00:12:46.320
Sadly, the superstar passed away in August 2022,&nbsp;
and the impact was felt worldwide. Unsurprisingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:50.600
her former Grease castmates felt the loss&nbsp;
heavily, with many paying tribute to their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:55.560
late co-star. However, it was her Pink&nbsp;
Lady cohort Didi Conn, who played beauty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.560 --> 00:13:00.280
school dropout Frenchie, who got to have a&nbsp;
heartfelt last conversation with Newton-John.

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:04.880
The pair had remained in contact throughout the&nbsp;
years, speaking regularly up to Newton-John's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:08.760
final few weeks. Conn explained to&nbsp;
Page Six that they had their final&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:12.240
conversation while her friend was in&nbsp;
the hospital. Despite her condition,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:17.240
Newton-John thoughtfully spent most of the&nbsp;
chat concerned about Conn, who had also been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.240 --> 00:13:23.240
sick. She even sent her old friend flowers the&nbsp;
very next day, passing on shortly thereafter.

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:26.960
As one fourth of the Beatles, John&nbsp;
Lennon is overwhelmingly recognized&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:32.120
as a musical sensation. For the majority of&nbsp;
the 1960s, Lennon and his bandmates reigned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:36.600
supreme over the music charts, becoming the&nbsp;
most influential music group of all time.

00:13:36.600 --> 00:13:41.160
What some fans may not realize is that The&nbsp;
Beatles briefly parlayed their fame into Hollywood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:41.160 --> 00:13:46.640
stardom. During the height of Beatlemania, the&nbsp;
legendary rock group toplined two comedy films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:51.720
A Hard Day's Night and Help!, and they almost&nbsp;
starred in their own version of Lord of the Rings.

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:56.400
Of course, The Beatles separated in 1970,&nbsp;
10 years before John Lennon was murdered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:56.400 --> 00:14:00.680
outside his Manhattan apartment. Bandmate&nbsp;
Paul McCartney has openly admitted that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.680 --> 00:14:05.040
he was heartbroken that he could never fix&nbsp;
things with his old friend, saying to Playboy,

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:09.840
"I do feel it was sad that we never actually&nbsp;
sat down and straightened our differences out."

00:14:09.840 --> 00:14:13.640
However, McCartney confirmed that the&nbsp;
two were on good terms before Lennon's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:13.640 --> 00:14:17.200
passing. The pair spoke on the phone, and&nbsp;
they had a pleasant conversation about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:20.960
their families. Paul was happy to hear&nbsp;
that his old friend was enjoying life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:26.080
and making plans for the next steps in his career.&nbsp;
Sadly, those plans would never come to fruition,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:31.920
and any chance at a Beatles reunion was snuffed&nbsp;
out on that fateful December night in 1980.

00:14:31.920 --> 00:14:37.600
Unmistakable as gangster Henry Hill from the film&nbsp;
Goodfellas, Ray Liotta nevertheless established an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:42.320
accomplished career beyond mobster flicks.&nbsp;
Speaking with Long Island Weekly, Liotta&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:47.800
expressed that he tried his hardest to appear&nbsp;
in as wide a variety of projects as he could,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:52.920
which manifested in him starring alongside the&nbsp;
Muppets and portraying the likes of Frank Sinatra.

00:14:52.920 --> 00:14:57.880
So, it is unsurprising that Liotta opted to&nbsp;
take on a role in one of the most outrageous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:57.880 --> 00:15:03.040
and original films in recent years, becoming&nbsp;
the villain Syd White for the rambunctious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:07.520
Cocaine Bear. Tragically, it was one of&nbsp;
the last projects Liotta would finish,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:07.520 --> 00:15:11.680
as he passed away in May 2022&nbsp;
before the film even opened.

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:15.360
Before Liotta wrapped up his work&nbsp;
on the drug-infused-bear movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:15.360 --> 00:15:19.000
he offered some touching words to his&nbsp;
friends and castmates. The film was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:24.200
directed by Elizabeth Banks, who previously&nbsp;
shared the screen with Liotta in The Details.

00:15:24.200 --> 00:15:29.080
Banks remembers her last interaction with the&nbsp;
actor before he departed for another film set&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:29.080 --> 00:15:34.440
in the Dominican Republic. She told USA Today&nbsp;
the pair hugged, and Liotta expressed his pride&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:34.440 --> 00:15:39.880
in the outrageous movie they had made. Banks also&nbsp;
recalled another one of their last interactions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:39.880 --> 00:15:45.200
in which he complimented the performance of&nbsp;
his Cocaine Bear co-star, Alden Ehrenreich.

00:15:45.200 --> 00:15:48.520
Known for hosting the "Weekend Update"&nbsp;
segment of Saturday Night Live,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:52.640
comedian Norm Macdonald was taken long&nbsp;
before his time. Macdonald elicited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:52.640 --> 00:15:56.640
laughs with his ability to crack even the&nbsp;
most sarcastic comments without breaking,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:56.640 --> 00:16:00.920
and has gone down in history as one of the&nbsp;
greats in the eyes of many of his peers.

00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:05.360
The folksy funnyman went on to star in&nbsp;
movies like Dirty Work and Dr. Dolittle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:10.600
as well as star in his own self-titled ABC&nbsp;
sitcom The Norm Show. Sadly, the actor hid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:16.200
his terminal illness from everyone but his&nbsp;
closest circle and died in September 2021.

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:21.000
Norm Macdonald's death devastated the comedy&nbsp;
community. Many of his peers shared their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:25.920
condolences on social media. One of his closest&nbsp;
friends was Bob Saget, who had performed with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:31.440
comedian many times and even directed Dirty Work.&nbsp;
In a statement posted to his YouTube channel, he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:31.440 --> 00:16:35.760
recalled that he could tell something was up with&nbsp;
Macdonald in the weeks leading up to his passing.

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:40.960
Saget recalled that, shortly before his passing,&nbsp;
Macdonald texted his old friend to ask how he was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:40.960 --> 00:16:46.400
doing. Saget sent a brief reply, and got another&nbsp;
text a week later. This time, it simply said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:51.840
"I love you." Saget replied in kind, and the news&nbsp;
of Macdonald's passing broke just days later.

00:16:51.840 --> 00:16:57.920
Fans of romantic comedies will remember the&nbsp;
1987 film Moonstruck well. The MGM hit starred&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:57.920 --> 00:17:03.120
singer Cher as a woman falling in love with her&nbsp;
fiancé's brother, played by Nicolas Cage. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:08.040
movie collected six Academy Award nominations,&nbsp;
winning one for Cher's leading performance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:13.560
and another for supporting actress Olympia&nbsp;
Dukakis' performance as Cher's onscreen mother.

00:17:13.560 --> 00:17:16.920
Both actresses would continue their&nbsp;
successful careers while maintaining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:16.920 --> 00:17:21.440
a friendship to the end. Dukakis became a&nbsp;
regular in television films and miniseries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:26.640
building a significant filmography and earning&nbsp;
several Emmy Award nominations along the way.

00:17:26.640 --> 00:17:32.880
Sadly, she became severely ill and passed away&nbsp;
in May 2021 at the age of 89. She was quickly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:32.880 --> 00:17:38.080
honored by her former castmate. Posting to her&nbsp;
social media, Cher recalled how often she and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:43.280
Dukakis laughed together, and how fondly&nbsp;
Dukakis spoke of her husband Louis Zorich.

00:17:43.280 --> 00:17:46.480
Cher went on to reveal that she&nbsp;
had spoken to Dukakis while she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:46.480 --> 00:17:50.840
was in hospice. While the older actor was&nbsp;
struggling to hear or speak at the time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:55.160
a conversation with Cher seemed to perk her&nbsp;
up. Cher recalled in a tweet that she told her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:55.160 --> 00:18:00.760
old friend she loved her, and a gradually&nbsp;
weakening Dukakis managed to say it back.

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:05.080
Best known for his starring role in the first&nbsp;
four seasons of the musical sitcom Glee,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:10.720
Cory Monteith was a Canadian actor on the rise&nbsp;
before he tragically died in 2013. His passing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:10.720 --> 00:18:16.360
was full of sorrow closely tied to his on-screen&nbsp;
romance. Monteith met his long-time girlfriend Lea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:20.840
Michele on the set of Glee, where each&nbsp;
played the other's romantic interest.

00:18:20.840 --> 00:18:22.040
"Break a leg."

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:23.880
"I love you."

00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:27.720
Their off-screen relationship became one&nbsp;
of the most heartwarming stories of love&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:27.720 --> 00:18:32.400
in Hollywood. Monteith's unexpected death&nbsp;
hit his co-stars hard but they found the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:32.400 --> 00:18:36.640
resilience to deliver a tribute episode&nbsp;
to the actor in the fifth season of Glee.

00:18:36.640 --> 00:18:40.880
Michele dealt with the loss of her boyfriend&nbsp;
and co-star in a creative way. The actress and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:40.880 --> 00:18:46.040
singer wrote multiple songs about Monteith&nbsp;
and she told Seventeen that one such track,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:50.120
"If You Say So," was about the final&nbsp;
words that they shared. As she explained,

00:18:50.120 --> 00:18:53.880
"There are lots of different emotions&nbsp;
— if you could see this person again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:53.880 --> 00:18:57.280
what are the things you would want to&nbsp;
say to them? It's a personal story."

00:18:57.280 --> 00:19:02.080
In terms of what they actually said to each&nbsp;
other, the lyrics suggest that Monteith told&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:06.440
Michele he loved her, and then Michele&nbsp;
responded by saying she loved him even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:06.440 --> 00:19:12.160
more. According to the song, Monteith then&nbsp;
uttered the titular phrase, "If you say so."

00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:15.840
For anyone who owned a television&nbsp;
in the '90s and early 2000s,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:21.520
Steve Irwin is an unforgettable figure. Suited&nbsp;
up in his tan shirt and shorts, Irwin was the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:21.520 --> 00:19:26.480
premier wildlife educator and television&nbsp;
personality known as the Crocodile Hunter.

00:19:26.480 --> 00:19:29.520
With a heart of gold and a deep&nbsp;
appreciation for all animals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:35.080
Irwin especially focused on the conservation of&nbsp;
Australian wildlife as a zookeeper and longtime&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:35.080 --> 00:19:39.880
host of environmental documentaries. Often&nbsp;
sharing the screen with his wife Terri Irwin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:39.880 --> 00:19:45.080
the pair became international celebrities&nbsp;
hosting a slew of zoology programs and specials.

00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:49.680
Irwin brought zealous enthusiasm and&nbsp;
unadulterated passion to everything he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:49.680 --> 00:19:55.600
accomplished until September 2006, when he&nbsp;
died during an accident involving a stingray&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:55.600 --> 00:20:00.000
while filming a new documentary. Although his&nbsp;
admiration for reptiles was evident from his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:05.120
presentations, so was his love for his family,&nbsp;
especially his wife Terri and their children.

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:10.320
Sadly, the Crocodile Hunter had a sense his time&nbsp;
was short, and was considering retirement in his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:10.320 --> 00:20:16.200
final days. As Terri Irwin said on the Australian&nbsp;
Broadcasting Corporation's Brush With Fame,

00:20:16.200 --> 00:20:19.920
"I remember him saying to me, 'I don't&nbsp;
think I am going to film anymore;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:22.480
I think I am just going to&nbsp;
spend time with my kids.'"

00:20:22.480 --> 00:20:27.160
The last thing Irwin said to his beloved&nbsp;
family was "Goodbye," as he waved to them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:32.840
as they boarded a flight to Tasmania while he&nbsp;
remained behind to begin filming his final series.

00:20:32.840 --> 00:20:38.600
Veteran actor Scott Wilson amassed film&nbsp;
and television credits dating back to 1967.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:38.600 --> 00:20:43.800
Despite earning a Golden Globe nomination for&nbsp;
his supporting role in the 1980 film The Ninth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:48.920
Configuration, Wilson struggled to find much&nbsp;
notoriety in the acting game until late in life.

00:20:48.920 --> 00:20:52.920
The aging performer finally found success&nbsp;
and fame when he joined the cast for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:52.920 --> 00:20:58.080
second season of AMC's The Walking Dead&nbsp;
as farmer and veterinarian Hershel Greene.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:58.080 --> 00:21:02.600
Maintaining a regular role on the series for&nbsp;
three seasons, Wilson saw his star grow even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:02.600 --> 00:21:07.680
brighter in Hollywood and eventually landed&nbsp;
a main role in the Netflix series The OA.

00:21:07.680 --> 00:21:11.240
Sadly, it was at the height of his&nbsp;
celebrity status that Wilson passed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:11.240 --> 00:21:16.200
away in October 2018. As the shocking&nbsp;
news of his death broke it was almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:16.200 --> 00:21:21.240
simultaneously revealed that Wilson would&nbsp;
return for season 9 of The Walking Dead.

00:21:21.240 --> 00:21:25.960
The season debuted the next day with a touching&nbsp;
tribute to the late actor. Subsequently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:28.920
his co-stars honored the late&nbsp;
performer by remembering him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:28.920 --> 00:21:32.400
as a warm and entertaining man.&nbsp;
In an interview with MovieWeb,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:32.400 --> 00:21:38.120
his Walking Dead co-star Norman Reedus recalled&nbsp;
his hilariously touching last visit with Wilson.

00:21:38.120 --> 00:21:42.160
"He's sitting there next to me, and he can't&nbsp;
speak very well. I looked over at him and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:42.160 --> 00:21:47.880
he looked over at me, and I go 'You're such a&nbsp;
f---ing a--hole.' And he just starts laughing."

00:21:47.880 --> 00:21:53.320
Reaching icon status for his contributions to&nbsp;
animation and puppeteering, Jim Henson was the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:53.320 --> 00:21:57.760
creative mastermind behind franchises&nbsp;
such as The Muppets and Sesame Street,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:57.760 --> 00:22:00.720
as well as feature-length films&nbsp;
like Labyrinth. The voice and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:00.720 --> 00:22:04.200
performer behind Kermit the Frog and&nbsp;
a collection of other characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:04.200 --> 00:22:08.400
Henson hand-built a production company&nbsp;
that made people smile all over the world.

00:22:08.400 --> 00:22:14.880
Tragically, Henson died abruptly and unexpectedly&nbsp;
from a common bacterial infection in May 1990.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:14.880 --> 00:22:19.000
His death devastated the community that&nbsp;
he is credited with creating. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:24.080
the Muppet man did leave some final words for his&nbsp;
friends and family in the form of two letters.

00:22:24.080 --> 00:22:28.520
In them, he discusses how he does not fear&nbsp;
death, but instead looks forward to having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:28.520 --> 00:22:33.760
his curiosities about it satisfied, as well as&nbsp;
getting to greet old friends who passed on before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:33.760 --> 00:22:39.000
him. He encouraged his loved ones to care for each&nbsp;
other and forgive trespasses. The note goes on to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:39.000 --> 00:22:44.200
detail his wishes for his funeral, including&nbsp;
asking his Muppet family to sing "happy and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:44.200 --> 00:22:49.400
joyful" songs. Always the jokester, Henson's&nbsp;
final words are the most fitting. He wrote,

00:22:49.400 --> 00:22:53.520
"Have a wonderful time in life, everybody;&nbsp;
it feels strange writing this kind of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:53.520 --> 00:22:57.960
thing while I'm still alive, but it&nbsp;
wouldn't be easy to do after I go."

00:22:58.600 --> 00:23:02.520
"We will miss you, Jim Henson."

00:23:02.520 --> 00:23:06.840
One of the more recent heartbreaks to hit&nbsp;
Hollywood was Chadwick Boseman's untimely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:06.840 --> 00:23:11.000
death. Recognized for portraying Black&nbsp;
Panther in the Marvel Cinematic Universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:11.000 --> 00:23:16.400
Boseman was an award-winning actor who appeared&nbsp;
on screens as far back as the early 2000s.

00:23:16.400 --> 00:23:20.480
His death came as a surprise to most,&nbsp;
as he never spoke about his illnesses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:20.480 --> 00:23:26.800
publicly before passing away in August 2020 at&nbsp;
the age of 43. Upon the actor's shocking death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:30.720
his friends and co-stars were quick&nbsp;
to fondly remember the Avengers star.

00:23:30.720 --> 00:23:37.120
Josh Gad, who co-starred with Boseman in the 2017&nbsp;
legal drama Marshall, had a particularly special&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:37.120 --> 00:23:41.960
remembrance for his friend. Noting that the late&nbsp;
actor knew how important it was to appreciate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:41.960 --> 00:23:47.120
every minute we have on earth. Gad tweeted one&nbsp;
of the final text messages he got from Boseman.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:47.120 --> 00:23:52.240
The message, which was largely celebrating&nbsp;
recent rainfall in Los Angeles, read in part,

00:23:52.240 --> 00:23:56.840
"Inhale and exhale this moment, and thank God&nbsp;
for the unique beauties and wonders of this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:56.840 --> 00:24:02.120
day. We should take advantage of every moment we&nbsp;
can to enjoy the simplicity of God's creation."

00:24:02.120 --> 00:24:04.160
Boseman's final messages about living&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:04.160 --> 00:24:08.570
every moment fell especially heavy&nbsp;
considering the secrets he withheld.

